import Site from '../layouts/Site.astro';
---
<Site title="codemap privacy" description="Draft privacy notice for codemap.build and codemap Team. What is collected, why, where it lives, and how to have it deleted.">
<main class="prose">
  <div class="kicker">Privacy notice</div>
  <h1 style="margin-top:12px">What we collect, why, and how to have it deleted</h1>
  <div class="banner">Draft, not yet in force. Placeholders are marked.</div>
  <h2>Who we are</h2>
  <p><span class="ph">[SELLER ENTITY]</span> operates codemap.build and codemap Team. Contact: <span class="ph">[SUPPORT EMAIL]</span>.</p>
  <h2>This website</h2>
  <p>If product analytics are enabled, we record page views and the early-access form submission through PostHog. If they are not enabled, no analytics script loads. The early-access form stores the name, work email, repository URL, team size and stack you type, so we can reply. We delete a request on ask.</p>
  <h2>The service</h2>
  <p>When you install the GitHub App we receive your GitHub login, the installation id, and the repositories you select. Snapshots contain file paths, importer counts, PR numbers and titles, and bounded file text as described on the security page. We do not sell data, we do not train models on it, and no model reads it.</p>
  <h2>Where it lives</h2>
  <p>Vercel and Neon in the United States. GitHub and Stripe under their own notices.</p>
  <h2>How long</h2>
  <p>Snapshots for 30 days after the last push. Account data until uninstall or deletion request, then 24 hours. Billing records as required by law.</p>
  <h2>Your rights</h2>
  <p>Ask for a copy or deletion at <span class="ph">[SUPPORT EMAIL]</span>. Where the UK GDPR or EU GDPR applies, a data processing addendum is available on request and Provider acts as processor for repository data.</p>
</main>
</Site>
